tory\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and January to February came in under 90% of normal in 34 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025, August to September came in at 60% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 158% of normal there. Every one of the 8 grids had its driest year in 1963, with grid 25996 the lowest at 60%.</p>"}
